WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.176
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.476 --> 00:00:08.897
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.197 --> 00:00:16.459
Unit nineteen: Future Forms Review (will/going to/present continuous). Today you will choose the right way to talk about the future.

4
00:00:16.759 --> 00:00:19.307
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:23.662
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.517 --> 00:00:25.239
Will.

7
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.981
Will means for predictions and sudden decisions.

8
00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:30.817
I think it will rain.

9
00:00:31.417 --> 00:00:34.034
Your turn. Say: Will.

10
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:37.669
Will.

11
00:00:38.417 --> 00:00:39.418
Going to.

12
00:00:40.417 --> 00:00:42.927
Going to means for plans and clear evidence.

13
00:00:43.517 --> 00:00:44.808
I'm going to study.

14
00:00:45.417 --> 00:00:48.243
Your turn. Say: Going to.

15
00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.101
Going to.

16
00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:54.327
Present continuous.

17
00:00:55.317 --> 00:00:58.303
Present continuous means for fixed arrangements.

18
00:00:58.917 --> 00:01:00.591
I'm meeting her at six.

19
00:01:01.183 --> 00:01:04.161
Your turn. Say: Present continuous.

20
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.465
Present continuous.

21
00:01:09.217 --> 00:01:10.160
Prediction.

22
00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:13.509
Prediction means a guess about the future.

23
00:01:14.117 --> 00:01:15.687
My prediction is rain.

24
00:01:16.283 --> 00:01:18.518
Your turn. Say: Prediction.

25
00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:22.159
Prediction.

26
00:01:22.917 --> 00:01:23.732
Plan.

27
00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:27.157
Plan means something you have decided to do.

28
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:28.960
I have a plan.

29
00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:31.924
Your turn. Say: Plan.

30
00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:35.536
Plan.

31
00:01:36.283 --> 00:01:37.273
Arrangement.

32
00:01:38.283 --> 00:01:40.515
Arrangement means a fixed appointment.

33
00:01:41.117 --> 00:01:42.466
It is an arrangement.

34
00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:45.668
Your turn. Say: Arrangement.

35
00:01:48.533 --> 00:01:49.627
Arrangement.

36
00:01:50.383 --> 00:01:51.326
Decision.

37
00:01:52.317 --> 00:01:54.258
Decision means a choice made now.

38
00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:56.118
It was a decision.

39
00:01:56.717 --> 00:01:58.928
Your turn. Say: Decision.

40
00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:02.768
Decision.

41
00:02:03.517 --> 00:02:04.529
Intention.

42
00:02:05.517 --> 00:02:07.481
Intention means what you plan to do.

43
00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:09.816
My intention is to study.

44
00:02:10.417 --> 00:02:12.616
Your turn. Say: Intention.

45
00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:16.363
Intention.

46
00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:20.481
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.317 --> 00:02:24.199
Visal, tell me your plans for this weekend.

48
00:02:25.283 --> 00:02:34.577
I'm going to visit my grandmother, and I'm meeting my friends on Saturday evening. I use going to for a plan and the present continuous for a fixed arrangement.

49
00:02:35.683 --> 00:02:36.975
When do we use will?

50
00:02:38.083 --> 00:02:48.238
For predictions and sudden decisions: I think it will rain. The phone is ringing, I'll answer it. We also use will for promises and offers.

51
00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:50.572
How to choose?

52
00:02:51.683 --> 00:03:06.946
Ask: Is it an arrangement with a time and a person? Present continuous. Is it a plan or an intention? Going to. Is it a prediction or a decision now? Will. Sometimes two forms are possible.

53
00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.565
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:10.417 --> 00:03:15.272
Grammar focus: Future forms: will and going to and present continuous.

55
00:03:15.572 --> 00:03:16.759
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:19.554
I am going to visit my grandmother.

57
00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:22.554
I am meeting my friends at six.

58
00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:24.939
I think it will rain tonight.

59
00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:34.406
Will = prediction or sudden decision. Going to = plan or evidence. Present continuous = fixed arrangement with a time or place.

60
00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:38.870
Be careful! Don't say: I will meet him at 5 tomorrow.

61
00:03:40.833 --> 00:03:43.170
Say: I'm meeting him at five tomorrow.

62
00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:45.249
Use the present continuous.

63
00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:48.767
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:50.742
Which Future?.

65
00:03:51.042 --> 00:03:53.517
This weekend I'm going to visit my grandmother.

66
00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:57.682
On Saturday evening I'm meeting my friends at six o'clock.

67
00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:00.155
I think it will rain tonight.

68
00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:03.921
That was a sudden decision, so I'll bring an umbrella.

69
00:04:04.933 --> 00:04:07.223
My intention is to study every day.

70
00:04:08.333 --> 00:04:12.114
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:15.637
Look at those clouds! It blank rain.

72
00:04:15.937 --> 00:04:19.300
A, will. B, is going to. C, is raining.

73
00:04:22.867 --> 00:04:25.098
The answer is B: is going to.

74
00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:29.169
I blank the dentist at four tomorrow. (fixed)

75
00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:33.343
A, am seeing. B, will see. C, see going.

76
00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:38.760
The answer is A: am seeing.

77
00:04:39.917 --> 00:04:42.348
The phone is ringing. I blank it!

78
00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:46.650
A, will answer. B, am going to answer. C, answer.

79
00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.246
The answer is A: will answer.

80
00:04:53.383 --> 00:04:54.872
Which shows a prediction?

81
00:04:55.172 --> 00:05:00.149
A, I'm going to study.. B, I think it will be hot.. C, I'm seeing Dara at six..

82
00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:06.292
The answer is B: I think it will be hot..

83
00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:09.612
According to the reading, what will he bring?

84
00:05:09.912 --> 00:05:13.531
A, an umbrella. B, a hat. C, a book.

85
00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:19.101
The answer is A: an umbrella.

86
00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:23.103
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:27.621
Write three sentences about your future using each of the three forms.

88
00:05:36.417 --> 00:05:37.789
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:38.089 --> 00:05:49.431
I will probably be a teacher one day. I am going to start a new course next month. I am meeting my English teacher on Friday at four. Each form shows a different kind of future.

90
00:05:49.731 --> 00:05:51.475
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:52.383 --> 00:05:58.356
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and future forms: will and going to and present continuous.

92
00:05:58.656 --> 00:06:03.247
Today's value is planning ahead. Make a plan and take small steps every day.

93
00:06:03.547 --> 00:06:06.258
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

94
00:06:06.558 --> 00:06:10.174
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

